    "a1-title": "How the five HE5000 models differ",
    "a1-ex": "Mono, Standard, PLUS, Fort and Diamond, using only what the product images and drawings already say.",
    "a1-p1": "The HE5000 series on this site has five models. Occupancy is written only when the product image states it. Mono is a single-person chamber. Standard is a 2-person seated chamber. PLUS is a 4-person seated chamber. Diamond is a single-person rest chamber. The Fort product image does not state how many people it holds.",
    "a1-p2": "Mono has a side door, with the touchscreen, pressure gauge and emergency button on the front. Standard is a black chamber with a diamond-quilted interior and two seats. PLUS is a black chamber with a star ceiling and four seats. Fort is a white rest chamber with double doors. Diamond is a white rest chamber with a round door and a lounger, and its drawing says the body is joined from two sections.",
    "a1-p3": "This site does not state a pressure range, an oxygen concentration or a medical registration number. Those figures are not printed on the drawings we publish.",
    "a2-title": "Why the drawing is the size reference",
    "a2-ex": "Millimetre sizes are copied from each model's drawing. The product page opens the original PDF.",
    "a2-p1": "Every millimetre figure on this site is copied from that model's dimension drawing. The product page links the original PDF. A number from one model is not reused for another.",
    "a2-p2": "On the Standard drawing the body is 2070 × 1749.5 × 1616 mm. The oxygen generator is 714.75 × 736.50 × 471 mm. The air compressor is 1263.85 × 631 × 320 mm. The air cooler is marked 588.97 mm wide and 387 mm deep.",
    "a2-p3": "On the Mono drawing the body is 1730 × 1980 × 960 mm. The oxygen generator is 730 × 980 × 420 mm. The air cooler is 589 × 604 × 387 mm. PLUS, Fort and Diamond each have their own drawing. Open that model's page for its marks.",
    "a3-title": "What O2Magic is for",
    "a3-ex": "The companion app shows home-chamber status and keeps the record on the phone. It is not a medical diagnosis.",
    "a3-p1": "O2Magic is the companion app for a home chamber. It shows chamber status and keeps the use record on the phone. The Android package on this site is dated 2026-11-06.",
    "a3-p2": "A reading, or a short face scan you start yourself, is for everyday self-reference. It does not replace a diagnosis, treatment or medication advice from a medical institution.",
    "a3-p3": "Chamber readings stay on the phone by default. The message form on this website also stays in the browser and is not uploaded.",
